1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,900
Hey, wake up. It's nearly time for class to start. Mr. Yasuda? Don't say I didn't try, at least.

2
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,100
Let's go. We gotta hurry and get back before the bell rings.

3
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:22,880
Whoa. Yasuda's out.

4
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:23,320
Huh?

5
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,260
His hair is, like, crazy smooth and soft.

6
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:29,820
Stylin'.

7
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:35,040
Yasuda. Mr. Yasuda!

8
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:38,000
Was there someone behind me just a second ago?

9
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:41,400
Yep. Pretty sure they were senior students.

10
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,880
I have a feeling they were girls, too. And I miss them.

11
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:47,460
So, uh...

12
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:49,760
My class has started without me. Damn it.

13
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,880
Um, just so you're aware...

14
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:52,660
Aware of what?

15
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:57,700
It's your head. There's something wrong with it.

16
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,780
Yes, every day!

17
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:00,460
Huh?

18
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:05,880
But why'd you bring that up now, of all times? Can't you see I'm in a rush here?

19
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:07,880
You misunderstood, yet you're still correct.

20
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:10,060
Ah, I've got a class to teach.

21
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:10,560
I've got a class to teach.

22
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,800
But why how'd you bring that up now, of all times?

23
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:13,380
Likeanyone rien to do...

24
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:14,740
harderons...

25
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:16,740
That long, although I didn't understand,

26
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:19,700
Because it's just being used to by the reunifications...

27
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:49,680
Thank you.

28
00:01:49,700 --> 00:02:19,680
Thank you.

29
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:49,680
Thank you.

30
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:51,680
Thank you.

31
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:54,500
Seriously, is this a joke to you?

32
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:58,160
He's wondering if we're joking?

33
00:02:59,320 --> 00:02:59,920
Question.

34
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:01,680
So, um...

35
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:05,120
Do it?

36
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:06,260
Ask him, Hori.

37
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,580
It's not worth mentioning.

38
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:17,720
Well, your English score was as awesome as ever, Hori.

39
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:20,580
Uh, um, thank you?

40
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:23,720
Come on, brain, think of something to say.

41
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,880
Does that bother you?

42
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:27,640
No.

43
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:29,840
Sir?

44
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,520
Let me guess.

45
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:33,080
Need a potty break?

46
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:33,900
No.

47
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:34,900
But...

48
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,340
Ask him.

49
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:37,100
Ask him.

50
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:38,420
I believe in you.

51
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,160
The theme.

52
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,980
Um, what theme?

53
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,980
Theme for today.

54
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,920
Today has a theme?

55
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:53,960
Does this have anything at all to do with our discussion regarding exam grades, Miyamura?

56
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:55,940
Uh, no, sir.

57
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:56,840
It doesn't.

58
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:57,320
Spectacular.

59
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:58,580
Then sit.

60
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:02,020
All right, what's up?

61
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:04,680
You appear to be very distracted and confused.

62
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,340
It's all your fault.

63
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:10,720
I just had to go and oversleep.

64
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,700
What class are we on now anyway?

65
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,560
I'm sorry for being late.

66
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:16,280
Forgive me.

67
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:18,660
Ah, decided to grace us with your presence, huh?

68
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:19,900
Oh.

69
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:22,340
Oh.

70
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:29,180
Oh.

71
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:31,820
Okay, you're going to have to stop.

72
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:33,540
I can't live you this early, Yasuna.

73
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:34,160
Really?

74
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,560
I look dying.

75
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,840
Oh, my gosh.

76
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,480
Too funny.

77
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:41,940
Were you still, like, going to execute today or what, Yasuna?

78
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,040
What?

79
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,980
You all think I look cute?

80
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:46,620
Do you want to explain why?

81
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:48,480
Miss Lou, face your eyes.

82
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:53,300
The heck is this?

83
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:00,900
Teens, I swear.

84
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:03,720
If girls are going to play with my hair, I should be conscious.

85
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:07,280
I want to feel a gentle touch of their fingers while I'm wide awake.

86
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,740
There really is something wrong with this head.

87
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,240
Wasted opportunity.

88
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:15,900
Hey, Mr. Ajima.

89
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,660
You know where the reference room key disappeared, too?

90
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:19,840
I don't.

91
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:22,340
Try asking the one who's in charge of it.

92
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,440
And who would this fabled keeper of keys be?

93
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,260
Nakamine, last I checked.

94
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,360
In fact, I believe he used that room himself just yesterday.

95
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,360
Mr. Nakamine.

96
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:42,720
Will you please return the reference room key?

97
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,460
I did.

98
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,500
It should be hanging up where all the other keys are.

99
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:48,520
Nope.

100
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,240
It ain't there.

101
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,280
But I put it back.

102
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,480
It's not there.

103
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:54,440
That's so weird.

104
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:55,680
Hmm.

105
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:56,400
Hmm?

106
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:59,180
Oh, my bad, man.

107
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:01,700
Guess it's been stuck in my coat pocket since yesterday.

108
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:05,300
Why is this scatterbrain in charge of anything, let alone keys?

109
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:07,300
Well, I'm glad we found it.

110
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,680
You really are some kind of keeper of keys.

111
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:12,060
Oops.

112
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:12,960
Wait.

113
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:16,640
It's the key to my bike lock that I thought I lost over summer break.

114
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:17,820
Back during the summer?

115
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,540
That was two seasons ago.

116
00:06:20,340 --> 00:06:20,740
Thanks.

117
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:21,880
I really owe you one.

118
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,800
Now I can ride my bicycle again.

119
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:25,540
Good for you.

120
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,760
But I didn't do anything.

121
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:28,400
What a modest guy.

122
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:33,360
Maybe we should entrust the key to somebody else.

123
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:36,320
Did you block in any other keys you forgot about?

124
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:37,840
Hmm.

125
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:38,960
That's a good question.

126
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,400
Hey, it's Yasuda.

127
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,420
What's the other dude's name?

128
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:44,860
Mr. Nakamine.

129
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,920
He's the physics teacher.

130
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:55,940
Did that lab coat come with trick pockets?

131
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,240
Looked straight up magical.

132
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:58,960
That's a lot of keys you have on you.

133
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:00,460
Yeah, it's quite a few.

134
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:01,480
Not magic, though.

135
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:05,120
I could also pull a crap ton of keys out of my pockets, you guys.

136
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:08,200
This isn't a competition so you can tone down the aggression.

137
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:08,880
I know.

138
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:09,640
I'm just saying.

139
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:10,500
I could do that.

140
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,460
You missed one.

141
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:14,780
Must have dropped it before.

142
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:15,560
Good eye.

143
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,020
You just saved me a lot of trouble.

144
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:19,520
It's probably the key to something pretty important.

145
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:21,360
Uh-oh.

146
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:27,740
I'm not sure where the reference room key is now.

147
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:29,700
Mr. Nakamine?

148
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:33,960
Huh?

149
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:38,380
Oh.

150
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:43,720
Wait up!

151
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:44,640
Hmm?

152
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,780
You dropped all these.

153
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:47,920
Oh, gosh.

154
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:49,280
I didn't even notice.

155
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:50,620
Thank you so much.

156
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:51,480
Wow.

157
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:52,320
You're welcome.

158
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:54,460
But you might have a hole in your pocket.

159
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,000
Nah.

160
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,780
This coat's really sturdy, so...

161
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:04,000
Oh.

162
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:05,520
No worries.

163
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:08,060
I just happened to have a sewing kit with me.

164
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:09,680
Well, well.

165
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:16,140
You're quite skilled with your hands, young lady.

166
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,780
Young lady?

167
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:20,220
I'm Ushikawa from Class 3-1, sir.

168
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:20,780
Oh.

169
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:21,940
Right.

170
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:23,460
I'm sorry.

171
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:23,500
I'm sorry.

172
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:27,500
You know, to be fair, I don't teach Class 3-1.

173
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:31,300
True, but you did teach us when we were first years here.

174
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:33,680
Am I ringing any bells?

175
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:39,780
Ever since I was about knee-high, I've been terrible at remembering faces and names.

176
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:44,900
That said, I actually do remember you.

177
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:45,380
Hmm?

178
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:47,280
Hmm.

179
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:50,760
He-he-he.

180
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:58,060
An affair?

181
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:01,020
It should have been me in there.

182
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:03,160
Gosh darn that man's ditzy charm.

183
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:03,940
How?

184
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:07,440
How'd he get a teenage girl to sit in a closed room with him?

185
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:08,100
No clue.

186
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:09,680
Now shut the hell up and die, loser.

187
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,920
Casually demanding that people die is wrong.

188
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,240
You almost sounded like a real teacher for a second.

189
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:19,480
Gotta say, a sewing kit's the last thing I would expect someone as breezy as Yoshikawa

190
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,960
to have stowed in her school bag.

191
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:22,860
Well, that goes double for me.

192
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:25,100
Because...

193
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,500
Toru, where's your button, dude?

194
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,140
Oh, I didn't even notice.

195
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:31,180
Looks sloppy.

196
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:33,020
Make sure you sew on a new one.

197
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:34,620
Yep.

198
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:35,540
No help.

199
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:38,360
Me and my button-less cover left a fit for ourselves.

200
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,880
It sounds like she has zero love for you, man.

201
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:44,220
No different from some random lunkhead she passes on the street.

202
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:48,560
You don't know what's going on in that cute, kooky head of hers, so quit acting like you do, perv!

203
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:48,960
Hey!

204
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:51,400
Nakamine's the person who got her alone in the room!

205
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:52,280
Hate on him!

206
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:57,660
I can't detect the slightest scent of ulterior motives, criminality, or indecency from Nakamine.

207
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:00,080
You, on the other hand...

208
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:03,400
I'll have you know that my intentions come from a pure and wholesome place!

209
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:03,980
Ball!

210
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:11,240
You did it so fast, and it's such amazing craftsmanship!

211
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:15,080
From now on, come to me if you get holes in your clothes.

212
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:16,940
And take better care of those keys.

213
00:10:18,540 --> 00:10:20,660
Just wondering, but...

214
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:22,900
Do you always have a needle and thread handy?

215
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:23,520
Mm-hmm.

216
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:23,940
Yeah.

217
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,040
There's this guy I know who keeps losing his buttons left and right.

218
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:31,400
His dumb face doesn't tell me when it happens, though.

219
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:34,200
He's missing out on some first-rate tailoring.

220
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:36,020
Hey, thirsty?

221
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:39,220
How about I treat you to a drink to show my gratitude?

222
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,080
Thanks, but I'm still working on my peach tea.

223
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:43,080
Oh!

224
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:44,100
Know what I want?

225
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,260
Show me your hand.

226
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:46,040
Huh?

227
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:51,160
What are they talking about?

228
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,000
Again, no clue.

229
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,360
She finished sewing.

230
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:55,340
Now leave!

231
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:13,900
Tohru?

232
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,460
Well, well.

233
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,400
So, um, what were you doing back there?

234
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:23,820
Hm?

235
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:26,100
With his hands?

236
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:27,260
Yeah.

237
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:29,180
Indeed, huh?

238
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:30,600
I read his palm.

239
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:30,940
No!

240
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:33,800
Since when do you read palms?

241
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:35,600
Since recently, because it's neat.

242
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,980
Want me to read yours, too?

243
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,680
Nah, I think I'll pass.

244
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:39,360
Why?

245
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,360
Not like I'm mine.

246
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:43,260
Hmm.

247
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:45,340
Mm-hmm.

248
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:52,040
Your lines are super-duper mega-faint!

249
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:54,100
Mr. Nakamine's are the exact same!

250
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,620
Wait, that counts as a reading?

251
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:58,880
I thought you would say how lucky I am and stuff.

252
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:00,920
How am I supposed to know that?

253
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:02,860
Go check your daily horoscope.

254
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,240
Talk about a total cop-out.

255
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:09,500
Well, anyway, have you tried reading anyone else's palm yet?

256
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:10,500
Nope.

257
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,320
Oh, except for Hody.

258
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,220
Nice big and bold lines.

259
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,080
Why'd you ask?

260
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:17,760
Because people might think you're a weirdo.

261
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:20,760
Not that I do, though.

262
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:30,420
Wait, so getting into a hobby like fortune-telling makes me weird in here?

263
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:30,860
No!

264
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:33,160
Plenty of people read palms.

265
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,720
It's fun, not weird.

266
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:35,900
I know, I know.

267
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:37,020
Yo, Ishikawa!

268
00:12:37,580 --> 00:12:38,560
Good news!

269
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:40,280
Miyamura says he's in for tomorrow.

270
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:41,660
All right!

271
00:12:42,180 --> 00:12:43,740
Now, where should we do this?

272
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:48,360
I suggest we find an empty classroom, my old chum.

273
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,480
Don't call me chum.

274
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:51,480
I want in on the secret, too!

275
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:52,780
Oh, you know.

276
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,680
Just a little bro-tastic bro-fun!

277
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:57,560
Sounds dumb.

278
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:57,920
Really?

279
00:12:57,920 --> 00:13:09,700
I had a hard time sneaking in here.

280
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:10,540
Huh?

281
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:14,280
Oh, that thing is colossal.

282
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:16,980
Bigger is better, and we all know it.

283
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:19,380
I think looks are important, too.

284
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:20,480
No way!

285
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:22,860
Size is where the romance lies.

286
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:24,260
Hmm.

287
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:27,600
How's it hanging, adolescent boys?

288
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:30,260
Or should I say, what's got you so...

289
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:31,540
excited?

290
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,140
So, where you living nowadays, Yasuda?

291
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,840
Why ask?

292
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,500
You want to set it on fire?

293
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:40,840
I'm just curious.

294
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:44,220
You don't need to be curious about where your teachers live.

295
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,200
Besides, you three are in trouble.

296
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,320
You got that?

297
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,040
Sorry.

298
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:53,300
But, sir, I can't think of one school rule

299
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:55,580
that forbids us from eating cake inside a classroom.

300
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,020
Because bringing a cake that massive is unprecedented.

301
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:00,280
Oh, yeah, hey.

302
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,800
You live a stone's throw away from the school, don't you?

303
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:05,580
If it's the same address that I used for your New Year's card.

304
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:06,640
Ooh.

305
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,120
Are you planning to visit me?

306
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,600
Don't you dare!

307
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:12,880
And we aren't finished talking about your dumb cake!

308
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,520
Cake has lost our interest.

309
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,920
We wish to know about your lifestyle.

310
00:14:18,540 --> 00:14:19,280
Jeez, you're blunt.

311
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:22,160
Do you live alone?

312
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:23,820
Well, yeah.

313
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:24,940
Suppose I do.

314
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:26,360
Got a girlfriend?

315
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:27,740
Not presently.

316
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,500
But why does that even matter to you?

317
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,320
Because you're you.

318
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:34,620
The lewd dude who raves about his love for high school girls.

319
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,880
If you had a normal, non-spicy lady waiting for you at home,

320
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:38,900
I'd be mad.

321
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:40,120
Non-spicy?

322
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,860
Yeah, I feel that.

323
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:45,200
The thought of him in an average relationship is rough.

324
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:45,680
Right?

325
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:46,920
Luckily, I'm not.

326
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,140
So you're safe.

327
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,020
For now.

328
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:54,220
But if you land a perfectly normal, non-spicy babe, tell us.

329
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,260
What kind of woman are you imagining?

330
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:59,080
So you don't intend to get married?

331
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:01,320
I'm lacking a partner for such an event.

332
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:02,560
Are you keeping up?

333
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:04,500
Commitment's hot.

334
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:07,460
Put a ring on your normal, non-spicy girlfriend.

335
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,280
Guys, who the hell are you talking about?

336
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:13,660
Though I do want to wed before Nakamine.

337
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:14,580
So?

338
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,720
He's uber fixated on that dude.

339
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:18,800
Damn it.

340
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:20,760
You rope me into making small talk.

341
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:23,420
I really want to see where you live, Yasuda.

342
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:24,800
Same.

343
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,360
You jerks aren't welcome.

344
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,800
Unless you come knocking with your lady friends.

345
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,440
Ishikawa brings Yoshikawa.

346
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:32,580
Miyamura brings Hori.

347
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,800
And Iyurayu bring Ayasaki and Kono.

348
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:37,680
Then piss off.

349
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:42,440
Hey, what happened to that bright-eyed enthusiasm you had mere seconds ago?

350
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:45,240
You're the all-time worst.

351
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:47,300
No New Year's card for you next year.

352
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:48,880
I wasn't expecting one.

353
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:54,820
Speaking of expectations, I'm not sure how we look to you, but Kono and Ayasaki hardly tolerate me.

354
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:56,580
Oh, I see.

355
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:57,260
Sorry.

356
00:15:57,260 --> 00:16:01,020
Now, ask for the matter of the gigantic cake.

357
00:16:01,980 --> 00:16:02,380
Ah.

358
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:04,480
Hmm?

359
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:07,100
Never mind.

360
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:08,660
Go back to class.

361
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,360
Wow, really?

362
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:10,340
Woo-hoo!

363
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:14,120
Don't worry.

364
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:15,640
We'll visit again real soon.

365
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:16,080
Great.

366
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:18,880
But whenever you do, just remember to bring me some cake, too.

367
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:19,280
All right?

368
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:20,720
Total teacher fail.

369
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:24,060
Oh, but we are coming back for the cake after school.

370
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:26,020
Will you please keep it cold for us?

371
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:27,480
You bet.

372
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:28,440
Of course I will.

373
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:38,620
What kind of experiment is this?

374
00:16:45,640 --> 00:17:05,460
It's nine o'clock at night in the student council room.

375
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:09,520
The door's locked from the outside.

376
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:12,680
And there's a slumbering demon.

377
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,620
How could we both conk out so easily?

378
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:19,380
Is it drugs?

379
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,160
Did someone drug us somehow?

380
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:28,320
Well, regardless, it's best to let sleeping demons lie.

381
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:31,940
If I call the school, it should bring in the faculty office.

382
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:35,640
What?

383
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:39,160
Whoa, it's dark.

384
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:41,100
Ah, man, what time is it?

385
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:41,860
Do you know?

386
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:43,040
Time to die.

387
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:46,720
Oh, John, please don't panic.

388
00:17:47,060 --> 00:17:49,520
But it seems someone locked the door while we were sleeping.

389
00:17:50,260 --> 00:17:51,060
We're trapped.

390
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:52,060
Trapped?

391
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,220
How could you let this happen, you dummy?

392
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:56,640
Hey, you woke up a few seconds ago.

393
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:58,400
You're as much to blame as I am.

394
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,800
Well, this timing sucks.

395
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:03,060
I was going to buy carrots on the way home, but that's obviously out now.

396
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:06,260
I know the gardening club's growing a whole bunch of carrots.

397
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:08,060
Take some of theirs and be happy, okay?

398
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:10,360
And you call yourself our class president?

399
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:13,360
Your cell phone, call the school, or anybody.

400
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:14,860
Just hurry!

401
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:19,460
Is that how your mother taught you to ask people for help?

402
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:21,360
I'm sorry.

403
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,640
Please, hurry.

404
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:24,520
All right, chop chop.

405
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:26,560
What's the phone number for the school?

406
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:30,920
You should have that stored in your contact list!

407
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:32,280
Bite me.

408
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,880
Bet it's in the student handbook, right?

409
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:35,840
It is!

410
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,100
Come on!

411
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,160
Quit dawdling!

412
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:40,120
Why are you in such a rush, huh?

413
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,920
Is it because you need to use the dang bathroom, too?

414
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,140
Quit copying me.

415
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,420
It's a natural function!

416
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:47,060
Wait, you also have to go?

417
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:51,320
Honestly, what the hell are you two doing?

418
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:53,480
I was getting ready to head home, but...

419
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:53,600
Oh!

420
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:58,180
You could at least say thanks for saving us before dashing off to who knows where!

421
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:05,220
So, what kept you at school until this time of night?

422
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,060
He was out like a light, sir.

423
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:08,200
Now hang on.

424
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:10,060
This one was fast asleep, too.

425
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:11,700
Are you sure?

426
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:15,920
You weren't up to anything obscene, were you?

427
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:16,640
Excuse me?

428
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:17,880
Obscene?

429
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:18,560
Like what?

430
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:21,000
Freak nasty hoo-hoo-ha-ha.

431
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:25,420
Students will stay late every once in a while and get it on undisturbed.

432
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:26,480
Disgusting!

433
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:28,920
Don't let me in with all those nymphos!

434
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:34,440
And isn't this the fault of whoever locked the door to the student council room without checking inside first?

435
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:34,780
What?

436
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:35,800
Speak up.

437
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,140
I can't hear you, Sengoku.

438
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:42,320
You know, I do have other ways of figuring out if you were getting frisky.

439
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:43,580
Hori!

440
00:19:44,020 --> 00:19:45,960
Take off all your clothes right now!

441
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:49,000
What sort of situation did I stumble upon?

442
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:49,660
Oh!

443
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:50,840
Hello, Mr. Ajima.

444
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:51,960
Thank goodness you're here!

445
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:54,640
Check Sengoku for love bites while I check Hori.

446
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:56,080
It'd be the other way.

447
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:58,480
If it wasn't purely absurd.

448
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:01,720
We'll learn everything if we can see below the belt.

449
00:20:01,980 --> 00:20:04,160
All skirts and pants will be staying on.

450
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:09,780
I certainly hope you haven't used that excuse to do inappropriate things with other female students in the past.

451
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:14,220
Go home and have a good night, kids.

452
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:17,360
I need to have a word in private with this deviant, okay?

453
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:18,380
Okay!

454
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:20,220
Hang on.

455
00:20:20,340 --> 00:20:22,560
Deviant is a little uncalled for, don't you think?

456
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,380
If you'll excuse us!

457
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:25,480
Wait!

458
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:26,300
Come back!

459
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:29,040
Now, we're going to go over this in detail.

460
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:31,300
I need to hurry home.

461
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:33,680
The hallway's freezing!

462
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:40,380
Whoa!

463
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:42,360
You got locked in the student council room?

464
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,120
You should have called.

465
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:46,120
I would have rushed over to let you out.

466
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:47,640
I wasn't trapped long.

467
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:48,640
It was no big deal.

468
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,460
Were you all alone?

469
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:51,320
Or afraid?

470
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:52,200
Neither.

471
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:53,860
Sengoku was with me.

472
00:20:54,260 --> 00:20:54,780
Hmm.

473
00:20:54,780 --> 00:21:01,640
You okay, Mr. President?

474
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:04,100
I heard you were stuck in a room with Hori.

475
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:05,640
Did she do anything to you?

476
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:06,980
Not this time.

477
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:07,840
I'm fine.

478
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:08,980
Hey!

479
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,020
Do tell what you're trying to imply.

480
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,160
Um!

481
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:16,200
I meant the power dynamic!

482
00:21:16,620 --> 00:21:16,900
Right?

483
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:18,040
She's talking to you!

484
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:19,120
Leave me out of it!

485
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:21,260
Elaborate now, Miyamoto.

486
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,940
This behavior is exactly what he meant!

487
00:21:25,780 --> 00:21:26,300
What?

488
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:29,060
Be calm.

489
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,860
Please don't resort to violence.

490
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:35,360
Deep breaths.

491
00:21:35,580 --> 00:21:38,420
Have to process that anger and purge it from your soul.

492
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,200
It's a chance to improve yourself.

493
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:45,480
That can't be the real Yasuda.

494
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:47,380
A non-evil twin, perhaps?

495
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:49,100
No, that's the guy.

496
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:51,060
He just had a change of heart is all.

497
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:53,080
Compliments of her own Miss Tarajima.

498
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:57,160
That seemed more like a change of a person than a change of heart if you asked me!

499
00:21:57,420 --> 00:21:58,980
Maybe she brainwashed him.

500
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:00,760
I love that woman!

501
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:01,680
She rocks!

502
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:05,620
Life is precious.

503
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:17,380
All- بتをñochair deriva

504
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:18,740
옳発狂ani

505
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:23,860
じゃあ、こんなの多かったよ

506
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:26,980
って見せびらかしたもの

507
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:30,180
褒めてくれた君も

508
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:33,880
前から同じの持っていたの

509
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:38,520
わぁ、今さらそんなこと

510
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:40,520
Oh

511
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:10,520
Oh

